---
/**
 * Cloudflare Web Analytics (S16).
 *
 * The old site had no analytics at all — this is new. Cloudflare's beacon was
 * chosen because it stores nothing on the visitor's device, which is what the
 * consent rules turn on: no cookie, no localStorage, no identifier, therefore
 * no banner. A banner would be a bigger imposition than the measurement is
 * worth, and there would be nothing for a visitor to decide.
 *
 * `/privacy` states, as fact, that this runs. Do not leave the token unset on
 * production without editing that page: a privacy notice describing something
 * the site does not do is as wrong as one omitting something it does.
 *
 * It is the one third-party request on the site, ~7 kB, `defer`red so it never
 * blocks rendering and never runs before the page is usable. That is a real
 * cost against the budget in docs/performance.md, and the honest alternative is
 * server-side analytics (Netlify's, paid) which costs the visitor nothing at
 * all. Worth revisiting if the numbers are never actually read.
 *
 * The token is public by nature — it ends up in the HTML — but it is read from
 * the environment rather than committed, so a fork or a deploy preview does not
 * report into the club's dashboard. Set PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN in Netlify's UI.
 * Absent, this renders nothing, which is what happens locally.
 */
const token = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN;
---

{
  token && (
    <script
      is:inline
      defer
      src="https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js"
      data-cf-beacon={JSON.stringify({ token })}
    />
  )
}
